Guidance lives in `.agents/`. Read `.agents/overview.md` for architecture,
ports, invariants and known traps, and `.agents/conventions/core.md` for the
always-on standards.

Hard rules:

- A resolver is consulted only for input that never matched the 32-hex
  destination-hash pattern. A hash-shaped query that times out stays a
  timeout. See `.agents/skills/trust-invariants/SKILL.md`.
- `register` derives the target from the caller's identity hash. Never accept
  a caller-supplied target.
- Attested records (sig NULL) never replicate.
- Run `py -3 -m pytest tests -q` before claiming a change works.
- No emojis, no emdashes, no semicolons in comments or docs you write.
- Minimal diffs, stdlib-first Python, no new dependency without a reason.
- Do not commit or push unless asked.
- Before writing prose, read `.agents/skills/no-ai-slop/SKILL.md`.
